function auditWriteLlrLdpcSignalPath(path,root)
%AUDITWRITELLRLDPCSIGNALPATH Concrete frozen bit/LLR index audit.
cfg=auditCovarianceAwareSnrPairedLocalization20Config(root);f=fopen(path,'w','n','UTF-8');assert(f>=0);c=onCleanup(@()fclose(f));
fprintf(f,['LLR-to-LDPC signal path audit\n\n' ...
'Frozen dimensions\nK=%d information bits/codeword; N=%d encoded bits/codeword; codewords=3; data subcarriers=%d; streams=2; QAM bits=4; coded bits/OFDM symbol=%d; symbols/codeword=%d; payload symbols=%d.\n\n'],cfg.ldpc.K,cfg.ldpc.N,numel(cfg.data),cfg.codedBitsPerOFDMSymbol,cfg.symbolsPerCodeword,cfg.Npayload);
fprintf(f,['1. Information/CRC/encoding\n' ...
'For codeword c=1..3, payload information has K-32=%d bits. crc32Bits appends 32 bits, producing Kx1. ldpcEncode accepts Kx1 and returns Nx1. codedBits((c-1)N+(1:N)) stores each complete normal frame contiguously. No interleaver or puncturing is called.\n\n'],cfg.ldpc.K-32);
fprintf(f,['2. Resource and QAM mapping\n' ...
'capacity=Npayload*384=194688 bits. transmitBits is capacity x 1. Codeword c occupies resourceOffset=(c-1)*169*384 followed by indices 1:64800. Each 169-symbol resource block therefore has 64896 positions: 64800 useful then 96 random padding bits.\n' ...
'reshape(transmitBits,4,[]) groups bits [4j-3:4j] into one 16QAM symbol. qam16ModBits uses qammod(...,InputType=bit,UnitAveragePower=true). reshape(...,2,48,507) orders dimensions [stream,dataSubcarrierIndex,OFDMsymbol]. Linear resource bit index is b + 4*((stream-1)+2*((dataIndex-1)+48*(symbol-1))), b=1..4.\n' ...
'Thus stream 1 precedes stream 2 within each data subcarrier; data subcarriers advance before OFDM symbols. No transpose and no interleaver occur here.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['3. Padding\n' ...
'For each codeword resource block, positions 64801:64896 are padding. They equal 96 bits = 24 QAM stream symbols = 12 MIMO data REs. validReMask is formed by reshape(useful,8,[]) and all(...,1), then reshape(48,507). Padding REs are excluded from detector iteration and from useful LLR selection.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['4. EP output and sign\n' ...
'auditEpDetectorOjcd returns bitLlr with size [2 streams x 4 bits]. bitLlr=log(P0)-log(P1): positive means bit 0, negative means bit 1. auditMechanismOnlineReceive transposes this to [4 bits x 2 streams] and assigns llrGrid(:,:,dataIndex,symbolIndex). llrGrid size is [4,2,48,507].\n' ...
'No explicit decoder-path LLR clip is applied. cfg.llrClip=50 belongs to data-assistance reliability modeling and is not used by auditMechanismOnlineReceive before ldpcDecode.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['5. Serialization and codeword split\n' ...
'llr=llrGrid(:) uses MATLAB column-major order [bit,stream,dataIndex,symbol]. This is the exact inverse order of reshape(transmitBits,4,[]) then reshape(...,2,48,507). usefulLlr=llr(usefulBitMask) removes the 96-bit tail of each 64896-position codeword resource block. Codeword c is usefulLlr((c-1)*64800+(1:64800)). No transpose or deinterleaver is used.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['6. Decoder and decisions\n' ...
'ldpcDecode(codewordLlr,cfg.ldpc.dec,50,DecisionType=hard) expects Nx1 LLR with positive=0 and negative=1, and returns K hard information bits. The current receiver computes CRC over decoded bits 1:K-32 and compares decoded bits K-31:K to crc32Bits(payload). codewordPassRate is mean of the three CRC results; codewordErrorCount=3-passedCodewordCount; whole-payload codewordPass requires all three. goodput=passedCodewords*(K-32)/(507*Tsym)/1e6.\n\n']);
fprintf(f,['7. Offline truth audit\n' ...
'For diagnostics, decoded payload bits for codeword c are compared with scenario.informationBits((c-1)*(K-32)+(1:K-32)). This truth comparison is offline only and is not called receiver CRC. postDecodeBitErrorCount and syndrome/iteration fields are diagnostic; decoder iteration count and final syndrome are unavailable from the frozen MATLAB API and remain NaN.\n']);
end

